{131}}{4}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   -13 \\cdot \\frac{13 - \\sqrt{131}}{4} = -\\frac{169 - 13\\sqrt{131}}{4}\n   \\]\n   So the equation becomes:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{150 - 13\\sqrt{131}}{4} - \\frac{169 - 13\\sqrt{131}}{4} + k = 0\n   \\]\n   Combine the fractions:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{150 - 13\\sqrt{131} - 169 + 13\\sqrt{131}}{4} + k = 0\n   \\]\n   Simplify the numerator:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{150 - 169}{4} + k = 0\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\frac{-19}{4} + k = 0\n   \\]\n   Solve for \\( k \\):\n   \\[\n   k = \\frac{19}{4}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{19}{4}}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{19}{4}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:73"}
